/verify-shots/

# --- Dnipro 3D enrichment: the hand-baked Slice-0 sample now lives in bakes/enriched/sample/
#     (regen offline, no network: `node scripts/build-sample-dnipro-tiles.mjs`; moved out of
#     public/ 2026-08-13 so builds never ship it — audit B10). Covered by /bakes/ below. ---

# --- Dnipro 3D enrichment: the REAL bake outputs + Overpass cache (regen: `npm run bake --
#     --city dnipro` / `node scripts/bake/bake-osm2world.mjs --city dnipro-o2w`). Baked tiles are
#     derived artifacts served from R2 in prod; they live OUTSIDE public/ (bakes/) so a build
#     bundle never ships them — dev serves them at /enriched/* via the astro.config middleware. ---
/bakes/
/public/enriched/
/scripts/bake/.cache/
# Both bakers resolve `--out` against REPO_ROOT (`join(REPO_ROOT, args.out)`), so an absolute-looking
# scratch path like `--out /tmp/foo` lands INSIDE the repo at ./tmp/foo, not in the system /tmp.
# Ignored so a throwaway A/B bake can never reach the session-end auto-ship. (2026-08-26d)
/tmp/

# --- OSM2World "Slice 1.5" spike scratch (478 MB jar + .zip/.osm/.glb binaries — regen offline). ---
/scripts/bake/spike-osm2world/

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Demo-pin seed downloads (scripts/seed-demo-pins.mjs re-run cache) ---
/.seed-cache/

# --- Lean 4 proof project. THE WHOLE BUILD TREE — ~7.4 GB: the Mathlib git checkout, its prebuilt
#     .olean artifacts, and our own build output. Regen offline, no hand-editing:
#       lake exe cache get && lake build      # FROM THE REPO ROOT (see formal/README.md)
#
#     The Lake WORKSPACE root is the repo ROOT, not formal/ — IntelliJ's lean4ij plugin resolves
#     the toolchain as <ideProjectRoot>/lean-toolchain, has no override setting, and then runs
#     `lake serve -- <ideProjectRoot>`. `srcDir = "formal"` keeps every .lean SOURCE under formal/;
#     the build tree lands here, at Lake's hardcoded workspace default (`defaultLakeDir` is
#     documented "Currently not configurable"). Redirecting it with buildDir/packagesDir was tried
#     and MEASURED: Lake honours packagesDir for LEAN_PATH but still materializes dependencies at
#     the default, leaving a second 601 MB Mathlib clone. One location is the only sane layout.
#
#     THIS LINE MUST EXIST BEFORE ANY ROOT-LEVEL `lake` COMMAND EVER RUNS — `session-end-ship.sh`
#     does `git add -A`, and one `lake build` materializes gigabytes here in seconds.
#     Tracked instead: formal/**.lean, lakefile.toml, lean-toolchain, lake-manifest.json. ---
/.lake/
